{"p": "astropy/io/fits/scripts/fitsheader.py", "n": 514, "binary": false, "doc": "``fitsheader`` is a command line script based on astropy.io.fits for printing the header(s) of one or more FITS file(s) to the standard output in a human- readable format. Example uses of fitsheader: 1. Print the header of all the HDUs of a .fits file:: $ fitsheader filename.fits 2. Print the header of the third and fifth HDU extension:: $ fitsheader --extension 3 --extension 5 filename.fits 3. Print the header of a named extension, e.g. select the HDU containing keywords EXTNAME='SCI' and EXTVE", "defs": [["ExtensionNotFoundException", "class"], ["HeaderFormatter", "class"], ["TableHeaderFormatter", "class"], ["print_headers_traditional", "function"], ["print_headers_as_table", "function"], ["print_headers_as_comparison", "function"], ["main", "function"]], "alls": [], "imports": [["argparse", 6], ["sys", 3], ["numpy", 1], ["astropy", 12], ["astropy.io", 7], ["astropy.io.fits", 25]], "froms": ["__version__", "log", "fits", "CompImageHDU"], "rules": [], "first": "# Licensed under a 3-clause BSD style license - see LICENSE.rst"}
